---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<!doctype html>

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <BaseHead
      title="About | The Reliability Loop"
      description="About The Reliability Loop and Rahul Siddipeta."
    />

    <style>
      .page-hero {
        position: relative;

        overflow: hidden;

        padding: 82px 0 66px;

        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
      }

      .page-hero::before {
        content: "";

        position: absolute;

        width: 400px;
        height: 400px;

        top: -250px;
        right: -90px;

        border-radius: 50%;

        background: var(--lavender);

        opacity: 0.35;
      }

      .page-hero::after {
        content: "";

        position: absolute;

        width: 160px;
        height: 160px;

        top: -70px;
        right: 230px;

        border-radius: 50%;

        background: var(--pink);

        opacity: 0.1;
      }

      .hero-inner {
        position: relative;
        z-index: 1;
      }

      .page-title {
        margin-top: 20px;
      }

      .about-section {
        padding: 62px 0 95px;
      }

      .about-grid {
        display: grid;

        grid-template-columns: 220px minmax(0, 720px);

        gap: 75px;
      }

      .side-label {
        color: var(--purple);

        font-size: 11px;
        font-weight: 700;

        letter-spacing: 0.14em;
        text-transform: uppercase;
      }

      .side-line {
        width: 45px;
        height: 4px;

        margin-top: 15px;

        border-radius: 999px;

        background: var(--purple);
      }

      .content {
        color: var(--text-body);

        font-size: 18px;
        line-height: 1.7;
      }

      .content p {
        margin: 0 0 1.15em;
      }

      .content h2 {
        margin: 2.1em 0 0.7em;

        color: var(--text);

        font-size: 31px;
        font-weight: 700;

        line-height: 1.2;
        letter-spacing: -0.03em;
      }

      .content h2:first-child {
        margin-top: 0;
      }

      .principle {
        margin: 30px 0;

        padding: 25px 29px;

        border-left: 5px solid var(--purple);
        border-radius: 0 12px 12px 0;

        background:
          linear-gradient(
            110deg,
            var(--lavender-soft),
            var(--wisteria-soft)
          );

        color: var(--text);

        font-size: 20px;
        font-weight: 700;

        line-height: 1.5;
      }

      .topic-list {
        display: flex;
        flex-wrap: wrap;

        gap: 9px;

        margin-top: 22px;
      }

      .topic {
        padding: 8px 12px;

        border: 1px solid var(--wisteria);
        border-radius: 999px;

        background: var(--wisteria-soft);

        color: #5c435f;

        font-size: 12px;
      }

      @media (max-width: 760px) {
        .page-hero {
          padding: 62px 0 50px;
        }

        .about-section {
          padding: 48px 0 70px;
        }

        .about-grid {
          grid-template-columns: 1fr;

          gap: 30px;
        }

        .content {
          font-size: 17px;
        }
      }
    </style>
  </head>

  <body>
    <Header />

    <main>
      <section class="page-hero">
        <div class="site-container hero-inner">
          <div class="eyebrow">
            About the Publication
          </div>

          <h1 class="page-title">
            The Reliability Loop
          </h1>

          <p class="page-description">
            A technical publication about engineering systems
            that have to survive real production conditions.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="about-section">
        <div class="site-container about-grid">
          <aside>
            <div class="side-label">
              Written by
            </div>

            <div class="side-line"></div>
          </aside>

          <div class="content">
            <h2>
              Hi, I'm Rahul.
            </h2>

            <p>
              I'm a Site Reliability Engineer interested in the
              systems, practices and engineering decisions that
              make production infrastructure more reliable,
              understandable and recoverable.
            </p>

            <p>
              The Reliability Loop is where I write about the
              intersection of reliability engineering, platform
              engineering, distributed systems, observability
              and automation.
            </p>

            <div class="principle">
              Reliability isn't a destination. It's a continuous
              loop of observing, understanding, acting,
              verifying and learning.
            </div>

            <h2>
              Why this exists
            </h2>

            <p>
              Production systems rarely fail in perfectly
              predictable ways. Real reliability work happens
              when architecture, telemetry, operational
              judgment and automation meet unexpected
              conditions.
            </p>

            <p>
              I'm particularly interested in how AI changes that
              operating model — not simply by generating
              summaries or suggesting commands, but by helping
              systems understand incidents, make constrained
              decisions, verify outcomes and learn from what
              happened.
            </p>

            <h2>
              What I write about
            </h2>

            <div class="topic-list">
              <span class="topic">SRE</span>
              <span class="topic">Platform Engineering</span>
              <span class="topic">Distributed Systems</span>
              <span class="topic">Observability</span>
              <span class="topic">AI & Automation</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <Footer />
  </body>
</html>